      <repository-location derived-from='https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/Elevate/MethodologyandCountryClusters?rev=' id='MethodologyandCountryClusters' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/Elevate' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style />
      <size maxheight='1500' maxwidth='1400' minheight='1500' minwidth='1400' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98934' id='28' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98858' x='571' y='533'>
            <zone h='98934' id='26' type-v2='layout-basic' w='98858' x='571' y='533'>
              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='4534' id='3' type-v2='text' w='90929' x='8500' y='533'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='18'>   PROJECT ELEVATE</run>
                </formatted-text>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin-right' value='4' />
                  <format attr='background-color' value='#d61f26' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='43267' id='5' type-v2='text' w='98858' x='571' y='8600'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>This dashboard drills down on country performance with a focus on DH strategy subjects (Growth/Affordability/Choice/Profitability). </run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Shows the performance of a metric in the </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>country cluster rank</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> and it&apos;s </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>trend relative to the selected &quot;comparison time period&quot;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>. </run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Methodology:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Metrics:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Input metrics</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> (which DH side direct control is possible) effect </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Output metrics</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> (main performance drivers).</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Secondary variables</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> are indirectly effected/effecting kpis which can be checked regarding need.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Clusters:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Æ </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Countries are clustered in to groups based on their </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>GDP per capita</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>. </run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Commentary</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Æ </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>of a country will be based on </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>YoY performance</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> and </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>rank in cluster</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Color Coding: </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Countries are color coded based on their position between </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>1st and 3rd Quartile in their cluster</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>. </run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' italic='true'>Example</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>: For a kpi that has &apos;maximum&apos; value as &apos;Best in Cluster&apos;, anything lower than 1st quartile is RED, and anything higher than 3rd quartile is GREEN. The values in between are shaded accordingly.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Arrow Trends: </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Arrows show the trend compared to selected &quot;comparison time period&quot;, metrics are grouped based on if they are getting &quot;better&quot; (green, up) relative to comparison time or getting &quot;worse&quot; (red, down). </run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Data Specifications:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Time frame:</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Last 12 Months</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Sources:</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> All kpi calculations and definitions come from respective departments.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='11'>Views in Dashboard:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>1 - Country Score Card:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>      This view focuses on only 1 country and shows the monthly value. Circle color coding guides on </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>rank in Cluster</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> of a country, and </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>trend arrows</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> show if the value is getting better (green-up) compared to the selected &quot;comparison time frame&quot; or worse (red-down).</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>2 - Country Card - Detail:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>      This view focuses on only 1 country and shows the monthly value, YoY, vs Best in Cluster benchmarks with last 12 months trend development of the KPI. Color coding of values guides on rank in Cluster of a country, and arrows show the trend compred to selected time period.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>3 - Cluster Card:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>      This view shows all the countries in the cluster with all selected metrics. Color coding guides on rank in Cluster of a country.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>4 - Country Comparison View:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>      This view shows the selected countries with selected metrics, countries in different Clusters could be selected. Color coding guides on </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>rank among the Cluster of a country</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>, not among the selected countries.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Elevate has been developed by International Markets.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>You can reach out to project leads: Egemen Can Gok, Lalit Saini, Lovish Gupta OR slack channel: </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>#data-hub-intl-markts</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> for your questions and your needs.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>Abbrevations in dashboard:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>*BIC - Best in Cluster</run>
                </formatted-text>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
